"""Patina 0.33.0: a parapet has a coping (the factory's roadmap 324; the walker: "keep the aluminium, keep going on
the edges").

`framing.coping_orders` orders one `coping` a parapet run from Deli Counter's parapet slots -- over the whole wall
and 5 cm past both faces, the corners capped once, nothing past an Empty's party wall -- and
`framing.drop_capped_edge_strips` drops the roofline strips it replaces, counted in the manifest as `superseded`.
`coping` joins the opening keep-out's exemptions.

Proven: tests/test_copings.py fails on 0.32.1 (fails_on_old.out.txt); the clone's suite, 399 passed, 11 skipped
(suite_clone.out.txt). Seed 9082 built against this clone and Zoo's: every building with a parapet got 4 copings and
lost the strips along its top (the bank 42 of 64, each rowhome 14), the twin, with none, kept its 44 (the factory's
docs/findings/parapet_coping/).
"""
